t of the global  touring exhibitions called the art of  the brick it was designed by Nathan  Sawaya who got his first Lego set when  he was 5 years old he was since then  inspired to create some of the most  amazing structures one of his greatest  creations is this t-rex dinosaur which  is about 19 feet tall and made from  80,000 Lego bricks Nathan said that this  work boosts his creativity and reflects  the artists growth  he had one goal for his exhibition which  originally launched in 2007 the  exhibition features everything from  famous paintings to DC superheroes  Nathan wanted to make his art relatable  to both children and adults but also  take it to the next level and create  artwork no one has ever done before the  exhibition holds 100 objects and 1  million bricks we can't even imagine how  long it took Nathan to make these  structures this dinosaur really looks  like it could be placed in a Natural  History Museum the Loch Ness monster  building an impressive Lego structures  on the ground is one thing but building  them in water is even more fascinating  you've heard of the Loch Ness monster  right it's a legend of a giant sea  creature that lives in the Scottish lake  called Loch Ness this Green Monster has  never been really seen but the legend  remains check out this incredible Loch  Ness monster made entirely from Lego  bricks  while the Loch Ness monster might or  might not exist it doesn't mean you  can't use your imagination to bring it  to life in some way you can find this  Loch Ness monster in Disney World  Florida and if you do see it make sure  you take a picture it's amazing you'd be  surprised how huge the lego Loch Ness  monster looks in person its head stands  on 20 feet above the lake and it's  approximately 60 feet long although  we're not sure why you can see this  monster in Disney World Florida hey  since you have the chance you should  totally go see it of course you can also  build your own version of Nessie using  just a few bricks but the question on  our mind is will we ever see the real  Loch Ness monster Lego cars cars are  also a popular thing to make with your  Lego bricks and the best part is you can  make them small or they can be huge like  this car ever wanted to drive a lego car  we're totally jealous of this guy and  his amazing design  this car belongs to the 20 year old Raul  Oh ADA from Romania this yellow car is  the world's first fully functioning cars  made from 500,000 LEGO bricks  it's called the super awesome micro  project everything is made from LEGO  bricks including the engine which runs  on air although its top speed is only  about 18 miles per hour this is one of  the most creative designs we have ever  seen Raoul claims this car was only  possible to be done because of the  internet he met an Australian  entrepreneur Steve Sammartino who helped  him with the project and brought it to  life Steve said that he is teaching  Raoul about business and Raoul is  teaching him about physics he also  explained that the project got funded  with a single tweet although Lego cars  might not be practical or safe this is  one of the most amazing LEGO creations  we have seen we can't wait to see what  Raul builds next lego warship so far  we've mentioned sea creatures towers  cars and dinosaurs what do you think  comes next  Lego proves there is really no limit to  your creativity with this next design  this warship is called Yamato and it's  the biggest Lego ship ever constructed  it's 22 feet long and it took six years  and four months to complete it  absolutely amazing isn't it it's a  tribute to the real Yamato the largest  battleship that ever existed and it was  more than 862 feet long but this mini  Yamato ship was made from 200,000 Lego  bricks and weighed an impressive amount  of 330 pounds pretty good right this  warship had everything you would see in  a normal battle ship including army men  and some impressive weaponry it even has  a lego flag aircraft space planes and  smaller battleships the artist who  designed the ship cleverly used a lego  marketplace to source the lego elements  that were crucial to building the ship  these elements include the Japanese Navy  flag and the Imperial Chris stamps  emblem we wonder how the artist managed  to move this piece anywhere after it was  completed how cool is this we bet this  will give you some inspiration for your  next future Lego project and who knows  it might take you 6 years to complete it  Lego Colosseum another amazing LEGO  creation is the Colosseum and no it's  not the small Colosseum said you can buy  in the store this masterpiece  was built by Ryan McKnight a famous Lego  builder who creates award-winning  sculptures with nothing but Lego bricks  his nickname the brick man is  well-deserved just check out this  incredible sculpture this impressive  Lego Colosseum is made of more than two  hundred thousand bricks this Colosseum  was built for the Australians Nicholson  Museum and Ryan knew it was going to be  a popular sculpture on the Internet and  he was right this sculpture is over  three feet high and almost six feet long  but it wasn't as easy to build as it  looks Ryan claims that the Colosseum is  the most technically challenging thing  he's ever built it turns out building  something oval-shaped it isn't easy even  for a lego structure but Ryan's hard  work paid off because this project is  just as amazing from the outside as it  is on the inside just like in the real  Colosseum the LEGO version misses pieces  to represent the structures ongoing  decay through the years it's layout is  spot-on with gladiators and audience  soldiers and everything you find in a  real Colosseum we're not sure how long  this sculpture took to make but we can  imagine it wasn't an easy project good  job Ryan Lego pizza although it's  definitely not the biggest construction  from this list it doesn't make it any  less fascinating just a warning this  might make you a little bit hungry 